**Timeline against Joe's estimates.** Capability 2 "about two months" means the end of December, which only holds if FIS signs the SOW and configures the sandbox backend by early December; otherwise the sandbox, production-credential and UAT-proof stories slip into January. Capability 10 "about three months" means the end of January, which fits: all service work finishes in December against the WireMock stub, and January is the UAT end-to-end test with the real sandbox.

**The critical path is FIS.** Everything that touches the real OPF endpoint (sandbox first call, production credentials, UAT proof, UAT end-to-end test, FIS sample alignment) waits for the SOW. Everything else proceeds against the WireMock stub and the FIS sample messages.

