### Edit 143578, Implement acknowledgment back to PayX on successful submission

Title, replace with: Implement the Bank Wire Rail II API response contract for the PayX integration service

Description, replace with:
Wire Rail II is synchronous, so the acknowledgment to PayX is the HTTP response of the Bank Wire Rail II API call itself. This story defines and implements that response: the outcome class (accepted, rejected, technical failure), OPF's response code and error details, and the payment id and UETR, returned only after OPF has answered or a definitive failure has occurred. Conversion, validation and OPF rejections return distinguishable errors so the PayX saga does not advance. The contract is agreed with the PayX integration team (Pod 2), who build the service that calls this API after OFAC, and is published in the registered API specification.

Acceptance criteria:

- [ ] Response schema carries outcome class, OPF response code, error details, payment id and UETR
- [ ] Response is returned only after OPF's synchronous response or a definitive failure
- [ ] Conversion failure, validation failure, OPF rejection and technical failure are distinguishable in the response
- [ ] Contract reviewed and agreed with the PayX integration team and published in the API specification on Exchange
- [ ] Contract tests cover each outcome class

