Acceptance criteria:

- [ ] Stage names for the accepted, rejected and retryable outcomes are confirmed with the PayX integration team and recorded on the capability page
- [ ] A test payment on an outbound GPN wire in QA reaches the integration service, calls Bank Wire Rail II, and produces WIRECLEARING on a stubbed 202
- [ ] A stubbed 400 or 422 produces WIRECLEARING.STOP
- [ ] A stubbed 500 or timeout produces no stage and Arbiter replays with the same UETR
- [ ] Results recorded with the request and response pairs

